3. Lock out your arms at the top of the movement, then lower the dumbbells back to shoulder level.
4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.', '1700');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO exercises (id, name_fa, name_en, category, category_fa, equipment, equipment_fa, target_muscles, secondary_muscles, instructions_fa, gif_url, muscles_primary, muscles_secondary, instructions_en, source_id) VALUES ('ex_db_0376', 'Dumbbell raise', 'Dumbbell raise', 'shoulders', 'سرشانه', 'dumbbell', 'دمبل', 'delts', 'traps, rhomboids', '', '', 'deltoids', 'trapezius,upper-back', '1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body.
