3. Raise your arms out to the sides until they are parallel to the floor, keeping a slight bend in your elbows.
4. Pause for a moment at the top, then slowly lower your arms back down to the starting position.
5. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.', '0376');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO exercises (id, name_fa, name_en, category, category_fa, equipment, equipment_fa, target_muscles, secondary_muscles, instructions_fa, gif_url, muscles_primary, muscles_secondary, instructions_en, source_id) VALUES ('ex_db_2292', 'Dumbbell rear delt raise', 'Dumbbell rear delt raise', 'shoulders', 'سرشانه', 'dumbbell', 'دمبل', 'delts', 'trapezius, rhomboids', '', '', 'deltoids', 'trapezius,upper-back', '1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body.
