4. Pause for a moment at the top, then inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells back down to the starting position.
5. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.', '0391');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO exercises (id, name_fa, name_en, category, category_fa, equipment, equipment_fa, target_muscles, secondary_muscles, instructions_fa, gif_url, muscles_primary, muscles_secondary, instructions_en, source_id) VALUES ('ex_db_0392', 'Dumbbell seated front raise', 'Dumbbell seated front raise', 'shoulders', 'سرشانه', 'dumbbell', 'دمبل', 'delts', 'trapezius, biceps', '', '', 'deltoids', 'trapezius,biceps', '1. Sit on a bench with your feet flat on the ground and a dumbbell in each hand, resting on your thighs.
